## Pin definitions and mapping to .bench primitives

The original 6502-family MPU exposes (at minimum) a **16‑bit address bus**, **8‑bit data bus**, **R/W**, **SYNC**, **IRQ**, **NMI**, **RDY**, and **RESET**, among other pins depending on packaging/variant. MOS-family documentation includes pinout diagrams (e.g., showing `DB0..DB7`, `AB0..AB15`, `R/W`, `SYNC`, `IRQ`, `NMI`, `RDY`, `RES`), and describes how these signals behave. citeturn18view2turn18view1

